 "details": {
  "title": "Long Ago and Far Away",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Dick Haymes’s record with Helen Forrest, both choruses in his key, E♭ (F for the trumpet), concert B♭3 to D♭5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 109, free in the tag. Over the guitar’s intro, the song’s last line comes first, turning on C7♭9’s E and D♭. Then two choruses of the tune as written, with breaths where the singers take them; in the second, over the guitar’s A♭ minor 7 near the end, G♭ in place of G. In the tag the trumpet sings over the record’s chords: A♭ over the suspended E♭, the line “all I longed for” again, a rest while the strings climb, and four notes alone down to the last E♭.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Jerome Kern and Ira Gershwin (1944)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, on the Fret Finder page’s chords and form; the intro line and the tag are set for the trumpet"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "E♭ major concert (F for the trumpet), Haymes’s key"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, two choruses (A B A C), tag"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (lafa-guitar.mp3), 3:15"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The five intro bars come first, so bar 1 of the Fret Finder page is bar 6 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
